  "scope": "All finite sequence lengths, including zero, over a commutative ring with native Koszul regularity; arbitrary N and HasExt universe. Exact top-class kernel is I\u2022N and the actual quotient N/IN computes native top Ext, linearly over R/I. Empty sequence specializes to I=0 and degree-zero Ext.",
  "upstream_audit": "Mathlib ProjectiveResolution.extMk_eq_zero_iff provides positive-degree boundary criterion only. Its CohomologyClass/Cocycle.toSingleMk_mem_coboundaries_iff and native cochainComplex.IsStrictlyLE 0 directly prove the degree-zero injectivity lemma. Existing Stacks topEquiv_topGen supplies coefficient detection. Positive-length kernel/equivalence are reused from Colib.TopExtCoefficients.",
  "new_generic_lemma": "CategoryTheory.ProjectiveResolution.extMk_zero_eq_zero_iff, any abelian category/HasExt universe/projective resolution. Degree-zero cocycle represents zero iff its map is zero.",
  "declarations": [
    "Koszul.seqTopExtClass_empty_eq_zero_iff",
    "Koszul.seqTopExtClass_ker_all",
    "Koszul.seqTopExtLinearEquivAll",
    "Koszul.seqTopExtLinearEquivAll_apply_mk",
    "Koszul.seqTopExtQuotientLinearEquivAll",
    "Koszul.seqTopExtQuotientLinearEquivAll_apply_mk",
    "Koszul.seqTopExtQuotientLinearEquivAll_succ"
  ],
  "reuse": "The positive-length quotient-linear branch literally returns the existing seqTopExtQuotientLinearEquiv, with a definitional equality theorem. No second complex, Ext type, quotient action, or positive-length kernel proof is introduced.",
  "limits": [
    "This unifies the native class, not a compiled identification with an old Aglib named cocycle.",
    "No Aglib environment/cache recovery or kernel replay.",
    "Shared integration and Library registration remain parent-owned.",
    "All-length naturality and toAddEquiv compatibility endpoints are not supplied by this increment."
  ],
